<main id="main">
<section class="story-scene hero" id="hero" data-title="Meghalaya" style="--length:1.35" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
<div class="story-frame">
<div class="hero-centre scene-copy"><div class="eyebrow centred">A story that begins in Jowai</div><h1 id="hero-title">MEGHALAYA</h1><div class="hero-location"><span class="pin-dot"></span> INDIA <span class="rule"></span> 25.45&deg; N &nbsp; 92.20&deg; E</div></div>
<div class="hero-bottom scene-copy"><p class="hero-thought">A new generation.<br><em>A world of possibility.</em></p><div class="hero-side"><p>Growing up in a world<br>that is changing faster than ever.</p><button class="text-button" data-jump="silicon">Follow the story <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></button></div></div>
<div class="landscape-note">Illustrated Meghalaya-inspired terrain</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="story-scene silicon" id="silicon" data-title="Silicon Valley" style="--length:2.1" aria-labelledby="silicon-title">
<div class="story-frame"><div class="scene-copy editorial-copy"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Silicon Valley, California</div><h2 id="silicon-title">AI is changing<br>how we learn.<br><em>And how we work.</em></h2><p class="body-copy">New ways to understand a difficult idea.<br>To create something. To solve a problem.</p><p class="body-copy quieter">The story may take us to a technology hub.<br>Its possibilities reach much further.</p><div class="word-row" aria-label="Learn, create, solve"><span>LEARN</span><span>CREATE</span><span>SOLVE</span></div></div><div class="map-route" aria-hidden="true"><span>JOWAI</span><div><i></i></div><span>SILICON VALLEY</span></div></div>
</section>
<section class="story-scene home" id="home" data-title="Back to Jowai" style="--length:2.0" aria-labelledby="home-title">
<div class="story-frame"><div class="scene-copy editorial-copy"><div class="eyebrow">02 / Back to Meghalaya</div><h2 id="home-title">What could this<br>mean for a child<br><em>growing up here?</em></h2><p class="body-copy">In Jowai, that future starts with something small: a question, a teacher, and the chance to try.</p><div class="editorial-note">Not just hearing about AI.<br><strong>Learning what to do with it.</strong></div></div><div class="map-route" aria-hidden="true"><span>SILICON VALLEY</span><div><i></i></div><span>JOWAI</span></div></div>
</section>
<section class="story-scene student" id="student" data-title="Meet Ari" style="--length:1.65" aria-labelledby="student-title">
<div class="story-frame"><div class="scene-copy editorial-copy"><div class="eyebrow">03 / One student. So many questions.</div><h2 id="student-title">Meet Ari.<br><em>He has questions.</em></h2><p class="body-copy">Imagine a Class 7 student in Jowai. Curious about a maths problem, a story, and what he might become.</p><div class="student-thought" aria-live="polite"><span class="quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span><p id="ari-question">Can you help me understand<br>why this works?</p></div><div class="question-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Explore Ari's questions"><button aria-pressed="true" data-question="0">Learn</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-question="1">Create</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-question="2">Discover</button></div><p class="micro-note">Ari is a fictional student, not a case study.<br>You will meet this same boy in the classroom.</p></div><div class="character-tag" aria-hidden="true"><span class="tag-line"></span><span>ARI<br><small>CLASS 7 / JOWAI</small></span></div></div>
</section>
<section class="gap-section" id="gap" data-title="The exposure gap" aria-labelledby="gap-title">
<div class="section-inner"><div class="gap-heading"><div class="eyebrow centred">04 / The opportunity to encounter</div><h2 id="gap-title">The gap isn&rsquo;t curiosity.<br><em>It&rsquo;s exposure.</em></h2><p>The same student. Different opportunities to experience what is possible.</p></div><div class="comparison-stage"><canvas id="gap-canvas" data-contained="true" aria-label="Two identical students at desks. One has opportunities to learn, create and explore; the other has fewer opportunities to encounter AI."></canvas><div class="comparison-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><div class="comparison-captions"><div><span class="mini-label">WITH OPPORTUNITY</span><h3>A world to explore</h3><p>Learn. Create. Experiment.<br>Discover what is possible.</p></div><div><span class="mini-label">WITHOUT THAT ENCOUNTER</span><h3>A world out of view</h3><p>The same curiosity.<br>Fewer chances to explore AI.</p></div></div><p class="comparison-disclaimer">Conceptual environments &mdash; not a comparison of measured student outcomes.</p><button class="text-button gap-next" data-jump="classroom">So, what could a first encounter look like? <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></button></div>
</section>
<section class="classroom-section" id="classroom" data-title="Inside the classroom" aria-labelledby="classroom-title">
<div class="section-inner"><div class="classroom-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / Same boy. A new opportunity.</div><h2 id="classroom-title">Step into<br><em>Ari&rsquo;s classroom.</em></h2></div><div class="classroom-intro"><p>The teacher leads.<br>Ari thinks. AI helps him explore.</p><span>Try a lesson. Ask with Ari. Check the answer together.</span></div></div>
<div class="classroom-grid">
<div class="classroom-visual" id="classroom-visual"><div class="room-topline"><span><i></i>A POSSIBLE CLASSROOM IN JOWAI</span><button id="reset-camera" aria-label="Reset the classroom view" title="Reset view"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7a6 6 0 1 1 0 6M4 3v4h4"/></svg></button></div><canvas id="classroom-canvas" data-contained="true" tabindex="0" aria-label="Interactive 3D classroom. Drag left or right, or use the arrow keys to look around. Ari is seated at a desk with an AI tablet. A teacher stands at the board."></canvas><div id="room-hotspots"><button class="room-hotspot" data-focus="teacher"><span class="hotspot-dot"></span>Teacher</button><button class="room-hotspot" data-focus="ari"><span class="hotspot-dot"></span>Ari</button><button class="room-hotspot" data-focus="ai"><span class="hotspot-dot"></span>AI assistant</button></div><div class="room-bottomline"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m5 3-4 4 4 4m14-8 4 4-4 4M1 7h22"/></svg>Drag to look around</span><span id="room-action">THE TEACHER SETS THE QUESTION</span></div></div>
<div class="lesson-panel"><div class="lesson-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Classroom activities"><button role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="lesson-content" id="tab-learn" data-lesson="learn">Learn</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="lesson-content" id="tab-create" data-lesson="create" tabindex="-1">Create</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="lesson-content" id="tab-solve" data-lesson="solve" tabindex="-1">Solve</button></div><div class="lesson-progress" aria-label="Lesson stages"><span data-step="0" class="active">01 ASK</span><i></i><span data-step="1">02 THINK</span><i></i><span data-step="2">03 CHECK</span></div><div id="lesson-content" class="lesson-content" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-learn"></div><p id="lesson-announcement" class="sr-only" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="simulation-note"><span aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Scripted demonstration &middot; not a live AI service</div></div>
</div>
<div class="classroom-principle"><span>AI supports the learning.</span><strong>It does not replace the teacher &mdash; or Ari&rsquo;s thinking.</strong></div></div>
</section>
<section class="programme-section" id="programme" data-title="The programme" aria-labelledby="programme-title">
<div class="section-inner"><div class="programme-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">06 / JSM Aspire Academy &middot; Proposed pilot</div><h2 id="programme-title">District<br><em>AI-Ready Schools.</em></h2></div><div class="programme-pitch"><h3>Train teachers.<br>Activate classrooms.<br>Open possibilities.</h3><p>A practical district-level programme for Classes 6&ndash;10: equip teachers to make AI useful for learning, creativity, exploration, career discovery and everyday problem-solving.</p></div></div>
<div class="pilot-metrics"><div><strong>25</strong><span>Schools in the<br>proposed pilot</span></div><div><strong>100</strong><span>Teachers equipped<br>to lead AI activities</span></div><div><strong>500<span>+</span></strong><span>Students to receive<br>guided, hands-on exposure</span></div><div><strong>32.5<span>h</span></strong><span>Practical teacher training<br>per cohort</span></div></div>
<p class="pilot-caveat">Illustrative planning assumptions, not delivered results. Final coverage, schedule and investment to be agreed with the district.</p>
<div class="programme-subheading"><h3>From a training room<br><em>to a classroom habit.</em></h3><p>Four cohorts of 25 teachers. A toolkit they keep.<br>Classroom use that continues beyond the training days.</p></div>
<div class="delivery-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Explore the pilot delivery stages"><button role="tab" id="delivery-select" aria-controls="delivery-detail" aria-selected="true" data-delivery="0"><span>01 / 2&ndash;3 WEEKS</span><strong>Select</strong><small>Schools &amp; teachers</small></button><button role="tab" id="delivery-train" aria-controls="delivery-detail" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-delivery="1"><span>02 / 32.5 HOURS</span><strong>Train</strong><small>Practical teacher capability</small></button><button role="tab" id="delivery-activate" aria-controls="delivery-detail" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-delivery="2"><span>03 / 4&ndash;8 WEEKS</span><strong>Activate</strong><small>Guided classroom experiences</small></button><button role="tab" id="delivery-measure" aria-controls="delivery-detail" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-delivery="3"><span>04 / 1&ndash;2 WEEKS</span><strong>Measure</strong><small>Evidence for what comes next</small></button></div>
<div id="delivery-detail" class="delivery-detail" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="delivery-select"><span class="detail-number">01</span><div><h4>Start with the district&rsquo;s priorities.</h4><p>The district nominates schools and teachers, confirms the academic calendar, and helps coordinate a suitable venue. The proposed coverage is refined together before delivery.</p></div></div>
<div class="programme-takeaways"><article><div class="takeaway-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</div><h4>A teacher AI toolkit</h4><p>Ready-to-use activities and a classroom action plan, retained by participating schools.</p></article><article><div class="takeaway-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</div><h4>A path to continued learning</h4><p>Support for relevant SOAR learning pathways. Enrolment, assessment and certification remain subject to course requirements.</p></article><article><div class="takeaway-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9636;</div><h4>A district impact report</h4><p>Teacher adoption, student participation and progression data to inform any future expansion.</p></article></div>
<div class="responsibility-strip"><span>Built into first use</span><strong>Responsible use &nbsp; / &nbsp; Verification &nbsp; / &nbsp; Privacy &nbsp; / &nbsp; Critical thinking</strong></div>
<div class="final-callout"><p class="eyebrow centred">From awareness to opportunity</p><h2>Let&rsquo;s give curiosity<br><em>somewhere to go.</em></h2><p>Begin with teachers. Bring it into classrooms.<br>Build the next step on what the district learns.</p><div class="final-actions"><button class="primary-button" data-open="pilot-dialog">View the pilot brief <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></button><button class="text-button" data-jump="classroom">Revisit Ari&rsquo;s classroom <span aria-hidden="true">&#8593;</span></button></div></div>
<footer class="page-footer"><span>JSM ASPIRE ACADEMY<br><small>DISTRICT AI-READY SCHOOLS</small></span><div><button data-open="sources-dialog">About this experience</button><button data-open="reading-dialog">Reading mode</button><button data-jump="hero">Back to the beginning &#8593;</button></div><p>Proposed programme concept &middot; Not a record of delivery or government endorsement.</p></footer>
</div></section>
</main>
<div class="story-footer" id="story-footer"><span id="chapter-name">A STORY THAT BEGINS HERE</span><nav id="journey-progress" aria-label="Story chapters"></nav><span class="footer-scroll">SCROLL TO EXPLORE <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></span></div>
<dialog id="chapters-dialog" class="dialog"><div class="dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">The journey</span><button data-close aria-label="Close chapters">&times;</button></div><h2>From a place.<br><em>To a possibility.</em></h2><nav id="chapter-list" aria-label="Jump to a chapter"></nav><button class="text-button" data-open="reading-dialog">Prefer to read the story? &#8599;</button></dialog>
<dialog id="pilot-dialog" class="dialog brief-dialog"><div class="dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">JSM Aspire Academy / Discussion brief</span><button data-close aria-label="Close pilot brief">&times;</button></div><h2>District<br><em>AI-Ready Schools.</em></h2><p class="dialog-lead">Teacher AI Upskilling &amp; Student AI Activation Programme</p><p>The proposed district pilot equips teachers of Classes 6&ndash;10 to introduce guided AI experiences in learning, creativity, exploration, career discovery and problem-solving.</p><div class="brief-facts"><div><b>25 schools</b><span>Illustrative coverage</span></div><div><b>100 teachers</b><span>4 cohorts of 25</span></div><div><b>500+ students</b><span>Planned hands-on exposure</span></div><div><b>32.5 hours</b><span>Training per cohort</span></div></div><h3>What continues after training</h3><p>Teachers retain an AI toolkit and classroom action plan. A 4&ndash;8-week activation period is followed by measurement and a district report. Interested students receive support toward relevant SOAR pathways, subject to applicable course requirements.</p><h3>What a district conversation needs to settle</h3><p>School and teacher selection, academic-calendar fit, device and connectivity arrangements, venue, delivery responsibilities, investment and funding route.</p><p class="brief-caveat">All pilot numbers are illustrative. This is a proposal, not a claim of an agreed pilot, completed delivery, guaranteed certification or confirmed partnership.</p><button class="primary-button" id="save-brief">Save discussion brief <span aria-hidden="true">&#8595;</span></button><p id="save-status" class="micro-note" aria-live="polite"></p></dialog>
<dialog id="reading-dialog" class="dialog reading-dialog"><div class="dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">The complete story / Reading mode</span><button data-close aria-label="Close reading mode">&times;</button></div><h2>A world of<br><em>possibility.</em></h2><h3>Meghalaya &rarr; Silicon Valley &rarr; Jowai</h3><p>A new generation is growing up in a changing world. AI is changing how people learn, create and work. The story takes us directly from the opening in Meghalaya to Silicon Valley, then returns to Jowai: what could this mean for a child growing up here?</p><h3>Meet Ari</h3><p>Ari is a fictional Class 7 student, not an actual beneficiary or case study. He is curious about a maths problem, a story and his future. The same boy appears in both the exposure comparison and the interactive classroom.</p><h3>The gap is exposure, not curiosity</h3><p>Two conceptual environments show the same student with different opportunities to encounter AI. This is not a comparison of measured outcomes, schools or districts.</p><h3>The teacher leads. Ari thinks.</h3><p>In the classroom demonstration, a teacher sets a learning task. Ari asks an AI assistant for a hint, thinks through a response and checks it with the teacher. Three scripted activities cover learning fractions, creating a story and investigating paper waste. They are illustrative demonstrations, not a live AI service or reported programme results.</p><h3>District AI-Ready Schools</h3><p>JSM Aspire Academy proposes a teacher AI upskilling and student activation pilot for Classes 6&ndash;10. Illustrative coverage is 25 schools, 100 teachers in four cohorts and 500+ students. Each cohort receives a 32.5-hour practical programme, followed by 4&ndash;8 weeks of classroom activation and a district report.</p><p>Schools retain a teacher AI toolkit. The programme supports progression into relevant SOAR learning pathways, subject to enrolment, assessment and certification requirements. Responsible use, verification, privacy and critical thinking are built into first use. Final scope, delivery arrangements and investment must be agreed with the district.</p><button class="primary-button" data-open="pilot-dialog">Read the pilot brief &#8599;</button></dialog>
<dialog id="sources-dialog" class="dialog"><div class="dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">About this experience</span><button data-close aria-label="Close sources">&times;</button></div><h2>A proposal.<br><em>Made tangible.</em></h2><h3>Programme basis</h3><p>Programme terminology, pilot assumptions, delivery sequence and intended outcomes are drawn from the supplied <cite>District Ready AI Schools - JSM.md</cite>, titled <cite>District AI-Ready Schools: Teacher AI Upskilling &amp; Student AI Activation Programme</cite>. Pilot numbers are planning assumptions, not delivered outcomes.</p><h3>Illustrative storytelling</h3><p>Ari, the classroom, teacher, dialogue and activities are fictional demonstrations created for this experience. They are not a testimonial, an actual school, a live chatbot or evidence of district-wide access levels.</p><h3>Geography and visuals</h3><p>The continuous 3D globe uses embedded Natural Earth-derived geographic outlines and a cartographic texture. It is a geographic overview, not street navigation. The Meghalaya terrain and classroom are original illustrative 3D geometry, not a surveyed landscape. No third-party child photographs are used.</p><h3>Privacy and motion</h3><p>The classroom uses preset local interactions. There is no live AI connection, student data collection or form submission. Motion can be reduced, and all story content is available in reading mode. Optional Google Fonts require an internet connection; no runtime map or 3D library is downloaded.</p></dialog>
